      "body": "## Motivation\n\nThe XPU manifest pins `torch==2.13.0+xpu` but currently selects `torchcodec==0.13.0`. TorchCodec-XPU 0.13 targets Torch 2.12 and can downgrade or conflict with the existing XPU stack. TorchCodec-XPU 0.15 is the matching release for Torch 2.13 and requires the corresponding base TorchCodec 0.15 package.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- update the XPU manifest from `torchcodec==0.13.0` to `torchcodec==0.15.0`\n- add `torchcodec-xpu==0.15.0` for Linux x86_64\n- preserve the existing Torch 2.13.0+XPU and Triton-XPU stack\n\nRelated SGLang-Omni PR: https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang-omni/pull/2312\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nThis is a dependency-manifest-only change and does not alter model numerics. Validation performed in the Intel XPU qualification environment:\n\n- dependency resolution retained `torch==2.13.0+xpu` and `triton-xpu==3.7.2`\n- `torchcodec==0.15.0` and `torchcodec-xpu==0.15.0` imported successfully with VAAPI-enabled FFmpeg 6.1\n- `torchaudio.load` decoded a 24 kHz WAV successfully\n- MiniCPM-o speech smoke returned HTTP 200 and a valid 3.72-second WAV\n- XPU manifest assertions and repository pre-commit checks passed on the rebased head\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable; this only corrects dependency selection.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests). (Not applicable to a dependency-only manifest change; focused manifest assertions were run.)\n- [x] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations). (No user-facing behavior changes.)\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed). (Not applicable to dependency selection; qualification results are listed above.)\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #35875428726](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35875428726)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #35875428712](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35875428712)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #35875428924](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35875428924)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
